---
/*
  Der echte Blocker der wertvollsten Gruppe ist die alte Agentur, nicht der
  Preis. 04-konzept.md Abschnitt 4.3, Seite "/switching".
  Harte Grenze, die in der Copy bleiben muss: einen Vertrag lesen und ordnen
  ist keine Rechtsberatung.

  Geaendert 07.09.2026 abends: hier stand ein Zitat in Ich-Form in einem
  blockquote, mit der Fussnote, dass es von niemandem stammt. Beide Dossiers
  verbieten genau das. Die Aussage steht jetzt als berichtete Beobachtung da.

  Geaendert 08.09.2026: jeder Abschnitt hat ein Bild, Ansage Manuel.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../components/CtaBlock.astro';
import Split from '../components/Split.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Switching agencies | Wunder"
  description="What happens when you are still signed with another agency, in what order, and where our help stops."
>
  <Split
    image="creator-tells-her-story.webp"
    alt="A creator talks and uses her hands to explain something."
    width={640}
    height={360}
    caption="Almost every creator we meet has been through this once."
    eager
  >
    <h1>Leaving an agency you signed with.</h1>
    <p class="lead">This is the part most people are stuck on. It is not the money.</p>
    <p>
      Most people tell us the same thing on the first call. They are nervous about telling their
      current agency. That part is normal, and it has an order you can follow.
    </p>
    <CtaBlock secondary />
  </Split>

  <Split
    image="lauris-speaking.webp"
    alt="Lauris sits at a microphone and explains something to the person across the table."
    width={640}
    height={360}
    caption="We read the paper with you. We do not call anyone for you."
    flip
  >
    <h2>What we do.</h2>
    <p>
      Send us your deal and we read it with you. We tell you how much notice you owe. We tell you
      when your next way out opens. We tell you what the part about your content means in real
      life.
    </p>
    <p>
      That is reading and sorting. It is not legal advice. We are not lawyers, and we are not
      yours. When a paper needs a lawyer, we say so. Then you take it to one.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not call your agency. We do not write to them in your name. We do not ask you to break
      a deal you signed.
    </p>
  </Split>

  <Split
    image="creator-meeting-blue.webp"
    alt="A creator and Lauris sit across from each other and talk in a studio with blue light."
    width={640}
    height={360}
    caption="Nothing starts before your old deal has ended."
  >
    <h2>The order things happen in.</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>You apply. In the form you say that you are still tied, and until when.</li>
      <li>We talk anyway. That call ties you to nothing.</li>
      <li>We read your deal. We work out the first date you can leave.</li>
      <li>
        You give notice yourself, in writing, in the window your deal allows. We do not start
        before that date.
      </li>
      <li>
        We start after your old deal ends. On day one we read your last thirty days. That is your
        starting point.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Maybe your deal has no way out for months. Then we say so. We put a date in the calendar
      instead of talking you into something.
    </p>
    <CtaBlock secondary />
  </Split>
</Base>
